  "pp_id": "PP-13565133",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "description": "CHANGE OF USE OF EXISTING STORAGE AREA INTO A SELF-CONTAINED STUDIO FLAT, WITH THE INSTALLATION OF NEW DOORS AND WINDOWS. ",
  "site_name": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - \r\nThe proposals by reason of design, size and layout would i) fail to provide an acceptable standard and quality of residential accommodation and living space and ii) fail to provide adequate outdoor amenity space, resulting in a cramped and unsatisfactory standard of accommodation to the detriment of the amenities of future occupiers. The proposals would therefore be contrary to policies CS 9 & CS.14 in the Merton Core Strategy 2011, London Plan 2021 policy D6, Policy DM D2 of the Merton Sites and Policies Plan 2014, DCLG Technical housing standards -nationally described space standard 2015 and the draft London Plan Housing Design Standards LPG 2021.\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - The applicant has failed to demonstrate that the proposal is capable of providing sufficient safe, secure and accessible cycle storage and refuse and recycling facilities and that these would not have a negative impact on the appearance and character of the existing building and its wider setting contrary to the following Development Plan policies for Merton: Policies SI 8 and T6 of the London Plan 2021, policies CS17 and CS 18 of Merton's Core Planning Strategy 2011 and policy DM D2 of Merton's Sites and Polices Plan 2014",
    "Reason : 3 - The development does not include a formal undertaking to ensure that the future occupiers of the development are prevented from being able to obtain parking permits for the Controlled Parking Zone and in the absence of sufficient on-site parking to serve the residential unit. The proposal would result in an increased demand for on street parking which would lead to increased kerbside parking, resulting in a detrimental impact on highway and pedestrian safety contrary to policies T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan 2021, Policy DM T3 of the Sites and Policies Plan 2014 and Policy CS20 of the Core Planning Strategy 2011.",
    "Reason : 4 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe applicant/agent was informed of any issues arising during consideration of the application but sufficient information was not forthcoming. \r\n\"\tThe application was considered to be fundamentally contrary to the provisions of the Development Plan and the NPPF, and there were not considered to be any solutions to resolve this conflict. \r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\r\n"
  ],
